title: Delete to the end of the file
chapter: 09
type: lesson
skills: op-linewise, op-motion
par: 12
minutes: 4
vscode: click, Ctrl-Shift-End, Delete
open: runbook.md

@brief
The bottom half of this runbook describes the process from before the
payment service rewrite. Following it now would corrupt the ledger.

Everything from the `--- old notes` line downwards goes. The three
numbered steps stay exactly as they are.

@keys
| `7G` | to line seven |
| `G` | to the last line of the file |
| `dG` | delete from this line to the last line, inclusive |
| `dgg` | delete from this line to the first line, inclusive |

@hints
The dead part runs from a line you can point at all the way to the end of
the file. You have a motion that means "the end of the file".
--
`dG` deletes from the current line to the last one. Get onto the first
dead line first.
--
`7G` puts you on the `---` line. Then `dG`.

@solution
    7G dG :wq<Enter>

Eight keystrokes to delete an arbitrary number of lines, and you never
had to know how many there were.

`dG` is your first *linewise* operator-motion pair. `G` moves between
lines, not within them, so `dG` takes whole lines — it does not matter
what column the cursor was in when you pressed it. Compare `d$`, where the
column is everything. The motion decides, always.

The pair of them is worth learning together:

    dG      from here to the bottom
    dgg     from here to the top
    yG      copy from here to the bottom
    cgg     wipe everything above and start typing

`dgg` is how you cut a file's preamble off in three keystrokes, and it
has a habit of surprising people who expect `gg` to be safe because it is
only a movement. Nothing in vim is only a movement once an operator is
waiting.

@start runbook.md
# Refund runbook

1. Check the payment service is up.
2. Retry the failed batch with `npm run refunds:retry`.
3. If it still fails, page the on-call engineer.

--- old notes, pre-rewrite, do not follow ---
Run the legacy script by hand from the jump box.
Then edit the ledger CSV and re-upload it to the SFTP drop.
Tell finance to reconcile manually before close of business.

